# COSMIC protocol descriptions

These XML files are the Wayland protocol descriptions for COSMIC's toplevel-info and
workspace protocols, as published by the COSMIC project (cosmic-protocols). Each file
carries its own copyright and permission notice in the `<copyright>` element, which
permits use, modification and redistribution with the notice retained.

`cosmic-combined.xml` is a merge of the individual files so that `wayland-scanner` can
generate interfaces and client code for both in one pass (interface names unchanged).

They are used by `src/cosmic_toplevel.rs` to know which window is fullscreen, which drives
the kernel's sleep policy. They are protocol descriptions only — no COSMIC code is
vendored.
